{
  "_readme": "INV-11 checkpoint ledger, as AMENDED by DEC-40. Every entry is WRITTEN BY THE HARNESS (RENDER_PERF_RECORD_SPLIT=<name> npx playwright test --config=playwright.viz.config.ts --project=chromium render-perf.spec.ts), never hand-authored. An entry records the split's MEASURED state, GREEN OR RED, per field: 0a and 0b are legitimately red because the decomposition exists to fix exactly the counters they fail. A null field means NOT MEASURED and is never filled with a plausible value. Structural thresholds and counters are monotonically non-regressing across entries; the writer throws rather than recording a structural rise. Asserted by TEST-P9 (src-app/ui/tests/viz-e2e/render-perf-splits.spec.ts).",
  "_provenance": {
    "_note": "METADATA added by the 2026-07-29 integrity sweep. This key documents the INSTRUMENT; it is NOT a measurement and no checkpoint field below was hand-edited.",
    "instrument": "Checkpoints 0a, 0b, A, B, C and D were measured with the TIP harness (src-app/ui/tests/viz-e2e/ overlaid from commit 750a3bd8) run against each split's own SOURCE tree in a detached worktree. This was necessary, not preferred: writeSplitCheckpoint did not exist until Split E (99caf80b), so the harness AT those shas was physically incapable of emitting a checkpoint -- which is the real reason this ledger held one entry for twenty splits. Checkpoints E and T were measured with a harness contemporaneous with their own tree. All eight are harness-written; the 0a-D six are instrument-from-tip. See DEC-40.",
    "gitShaSemantics": "Each entry's gitSha is the sha the SOURCE TREE was checked out at, captured by git rev-parse HEAD in a detached worktree. The pre-sweep ledger's single entry recorded Split E against cee51a59 -- Split D's commit -- because it was written from an uncommitted working tree; TEST-P9b now gates against that class of error.",
    "countersNotPerSplitFor": "F,G,H,I,J,K,L,M,N,O,P,Q,R,S -- no archived per-split COUNTER record exists for the twelve intermediate plane extractions; their counter evidence is wave-level runs plus the final full 15-test run at the tip. Structural coverage for them is gridDecomposition.test.ts's per-split ratchet. Gap left OPEN and named; see DEC-40."
  },
